# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include only what the build needs.
# This keeps secrets, .git, Terraform state and local tooling out of the
# build context by default, rather than relying on remembering to exclude them.
#
# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile, which is
# why this lives in docker/. The root .dockerignore is an identical copy for
# legacy (non-BuildKit) builders; CI checks the two stay in sync.
*

!app/
app/**/*_test.go
app/**/testdata/
app/coverage.out
